# Production values, merged over kubernetes/base/mlops-config.env.
# These come from Terraform outputs and change only when the infrastructure
# does, so they are edited by hand (unlike image tags, which CI's
# gitops-release job rewrites on every build):
#
#   terraform -chdir=terraform output rds_endpoint
#   terraform -chdir=terraform output s3_bucket_name
#   terraform -chdir=terraform output msk_bootstrap_brokers
#   kubectl get svc mlflow-service -o jsonpath='{.status.loadBalancer.ingress[0].hostname}'
DB_HOST=REDACTED-RDS-ENDPOINT.rds.amazonaws.com
S3_BUCKET_NAME=hotel-mlops-artifacts-production-REDACTED_ACCOUNT_ID
# Uncomment once terraform/msk.tf has been applied and the output above
# returns a real value (three TLS brokers, one per private subnet, comma
# separated). Left commented rather than filled with a placeholder host: an
# unresolvable DNS name here would make api/main.py's Kafka connect attempt
# fail slowly instead of the producer staying cleanly disabled, which is
# strictly worse than the status quo this line is replacing.
# KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=b-1.hotel-mlops-kafka.xxxxxx.c2.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9094,b-2.hotel-mlops-kafka.xxxxxx.c2.kafka.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:9094
# KAFKA_SECURITY_PROTOCOL=SSL
# Base list plus this environment's Load Balancer hostname: MLflow >=3 needs it
# on --allowed-hosts to accept requests arriving through the ELB rather than by
# in-cluster service name - opening the MLflow UI in a browser, or pointing a
# local `python -m src.train` at it, both go through the ELB. The previous
# deployment's ELB hostname is gone (a fresh Service means a fresh ELB, with a
# new hostname AWS only assigns once it exists) - add the new one here once
# `kubectl get svc mlflow-service` reports it, then let ArgoCD/kustomize's
# configMapGenerator roll the pods (see terraform/bootstrap/main.tf's sibling
# comment in Section 27 of the execution guide for why editing the ConfigMap
# in place would not reach the pods).
MLFLOW_ALLOWED_HOSTS=mlflow-service,mlflow-service:5000,mlflow-service.hotel-mlops.svc.cluster.local,mlflow-service.hotel-mlops.svc.cluster.local:5000,localhost,localhost:5000,127.0.0.1,127.0.0.1:5000,REDACTED-ELB-HOSTNAME.elb.amazonaws.com,REDACTED-ELB-HOSTNAME.elb.amazonaws.com:5000
